{"name":"Crossroads","hex":"#edd2a3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crossroads","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of crossroad"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place where one road crosses another; an intersection of two or more roads.","A centrally located position."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crossroads"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crossroads (1928 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Crossroads , also known as Crossways, Shadows of the Yoshiwara or Slums of Tokyo, is a 1928 silent Japanese drama film directed by Teinosuke Kinugasa. It is believed to be the first or one of the first Japanese films to be screened in Europe, and often mentioned in conjunction with Kinugasa's other avant-garde film, the two years earlier A Page of Madness."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f3/Jujiro_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crossroads_(1928_film)"},{"title":"Cross Roads (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Cross Roads is a 1930 British drama film directed by Reginald Fogwell and starring Percy Marmont, Anne Grey and Betty Faire. It was shot at Welwyn Studios as a quota quickie. It is a melodrama about a wife killing her unfaithful husband."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cross_Roads_(film)"},{"title":"Crossroads (British TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Crossroads is a British television soap opera that ran on ITV over two periods – the original 1964 to 1988 run, followed by a short revival from 2001 to 2003. Set in a fictional motel in the Midlands, Crossroads became a byword for low production values, particularly in the 1970s and early 1980s. Despite this, the series regularly attracted huge audiences during this time, with viewership numbers reaching as high as 15 million viewers."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c5/Crossroads2003c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crossroads_(British_TV_series)"},{"title":"Crossroads (2002 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Crossroads is a 2002 American teen road comedy-drama film directed by Tamra Davis, from a screenplay by Shonda Rhimes. The film stars Britney Spears, Anson Mount, Zoe Saldaña, Taryn Manning, Kim Cattrall, and Dan Aykroyd. Set in Georgia, its plot centers on three teenage girls on a cross-country road trip, as they find themselves and their friendship in the process."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/22/Crossroads_poster.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crossroads_(2002_film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3f/Crossroads_title_sequence_1969.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3f/Crossroads_title_sequence_1969.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Crossroads title sequence (1969)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrossroads_title_sequence_1969.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/ff/Crossroads_Kings_Oak.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/ff/Crossroads_Kings_Oak.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Crossroads Kings Oak title sequence (1987–88)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrossroads_Kings_Oak.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/bf/Crossroads_title_sequence%2C_2001.jpg/330px-Crossroads_title_sequence%2C_2001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/bf/Crossroads_title_sequence%2C_2001.jpg/330px-Cro